age and spoiled units cost much more than the missed sales they prevent.\n\n**3. Candidate 6 vs candidate 4.**\nCandidate 4 orders exactly the forecast, about 4.6% below average demand. That saves about 420 in purchases. But stock starts at zero, and candidate 4 runs out more often: roughly 35 more units of product 0 and 25 of product 1. Candidate 6 also has a better ending: on day 27 it orders [14, 19] instead of [23, 23], and those units would mostly be left over. Overall candidate 6 comes out ahead by about 100–180.\n\n**4. Candidate 6 vs 1 and 2.** Their middle orders are the same, so they differ only on day 0 and at the end.\n- **Day 0:** an order of about [47, 21] covers day-2 demand plus a small safety margin. Candidate 1 is weaker on product 1 (16), and candidate 2 over-orders (62/28), so extra stock sits in storage for a long time.\n- **End:** candidate 2 gains about 30 by ordering less on day 27, but loses more than that on its large day-0 order.\n\nMy estimate puts candidate 6 about 20 ahead of candidate 1 and about 35 ahead of candidate 2."}], "container": null, "stop_reason": null, "stop_sequence": null, "stop_details": null, "usage": {"input_tokens": 2, "cache_creation_input_tokens": 3682, "cache_read_input_tokens": 2269, "cache_creation": {"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens": 0, "ephemeral_1h_input_tokens": 3682}, "output_tokens": 5, "service_tier": "standard", "inference_geo": "global", "speed": "standard"}, "input_transformations": [], "diagnostics": null, "context_management": null}, "parent_tool_use_id": null, "timestamp": "2026-10-27T15:03:01.298Z", "request_id": "req_011CgSwYqLCidWk7zxvoRq8d"}, {"type": "stream_event", "event": {"type": "content_block_stop", "index": 1}, "parent_tool_use_id": null}, {"type": "stream_event", "event": {"type": "content_block_start", "index": 2, "content_block": {"type": "tool_use", "id": "toolu_01QhzGXGguVcUFRHzdYFvM9u", "name": "StructuredOutput", "input": {}, "caller": {"type": "direct"}}}, "parent_tool_use_id": null}, 