.\n\n**The candidates:**\n- **Candidates 6, 1 and 2** order the same totals (930 and 630) and only spread the buffer differently over time. Compared with candidate 4, the extra 46 units of product 0 cost about 110 and the extra 30 units of product 1 about 65. They also carry a little more risk of hitting the 172-unit limit. A starting buffer of about 10 roughly breaks even. Candidate 2's buffer of 25 is probably worse.\n- **Candidate 7** saves 14 × 35 = 490 in order fees. But holding each second day's goods one extra night costs about 580. Its large day-20 delivery (157 units) is also likely to overflow the warehouse, and product 1 gets cut.\n- **Candidate 0** (every three days) saves 630 but pays about 1,150 in extra holding, plus overflow losses.\n- **Candidate 5** (×1.15) builds up stock: about 1,000 more in holding plus overflow, especially on day 21.\n- **Candidate 3** (×1.25) has the same problem, only worse.\n\n**Why the confidence is only moderate.** Candidate 4 leads 6, 1 and 2 by about 150–200 in expectation. The actual result depends heavily on whether real demand runs high or low: in a high-demand month the ×1.05 plans win. I estimate about a 75% chance that candidate 4 beats candidate 6, and lower odds of it beating all three, since they tend to win in the same scenarios."}], "container": null, "stop_reason": null, "stop_sequence": null, "stop_details": null, "usage": {"input_tokens": 2, "cache_creation_input_tokens": 4669, "cache_read_input_tokens": 2304, "cache_creation": {"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens": 0, "ephemeral_1h_input_tokens": 4669}, "output_tokens": 8, "service_tier": "standard", "inference_geo": "global", "speed": "standard"}, "input_transformations": [], "diagnostics": null, "context_management": null}, "parent_tool_use_id": null, "timestamp": "2026-10-27T15:03:27.058Z", "request_id": "req_011CgSwWreGtafYuoHr4qmm7"}, {"type": "stream_event", "event": {"type": "content_block_stop", "index": 1}, "parent_tool_use_id": null}, {"type": "stream_eve